# ⛔ DENYLIST WAS THE WRONG SHAPE HERE — THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST ON PURPOSE.
#
# `run.py` launches workers with `cwd` set to THIS DIRECTORY, so a worker can
# drop any file it likes here and a later `git add -A` sweeps it in. That is not
# hypothetical: on 2026-10-19 a worker wrote `all.json`, a 72 MB dump of the
# whole corpus, and it went into a commit. Nothing was pushed, so it was amended
# out — but a denylist can only ever name the scratch files someone already saw.
#
# Snapshots and candidate dumps are excluded for the same reason plus one more:
# they hold verbatim memo content, and they regenerate from `GET /documents`.
#
# ⇒ Ignore everything; name the source files explicitly. A new source file must
# be added here, which is the point: it forces a decision per file.
*
!.gitignore
!run.py
!keyring.py
!select-all.py
!select-stratified.py
!select-dup-titles.py
!select-read-weighted.py
!select-split-candidates.py
!diff-stage.py
!with-grant-key
!worker-prompt.md
!credential-prompt.md
!consolidate-prompt.md
!README.md
!verify-run.py
